WEBVTT

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:41.280
So, the pilot captured by the
Capital Army is Raraiya Monday,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:47.030
and the unit she piloted was being used by
a pirate calling herself Aida Rayhunton?

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.030
Yes, sir!

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.160
The space pirate says
that unit is the G-Self,

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:55.540
but Captain Dellensen says
she's making it all up.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.540
- Yes, sir.
- ﻿Good work.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.510
Bellri Zenam, huh?

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.640
It's likely all a coincidence.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.600
This isn't the sort of thing
someone could plan out in advance.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.730
Yay! It's lunch break!

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.520
- You can run, right?
- Cheer girls, charge!

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:22.400
If you're looking into that
space pirate's Mobile Suit...

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.490
Our port, Hangar 25, is the place to go.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:29.530
Huh? That's where the
Academic Research Library is, right?

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:34.120
Bellri, you're the Operations Director's
son and you still don't know this stuff?

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.330
Well, the academy and Capital Guard
have separate facilities.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:42.300
The newly established Capital
Army is separate too.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:47.720
That's why the Army chose to hide it in the
academy's Hangar 25 while they study it.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.800
Why are they hiding and studying it?

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:54.810
Even though they know the suit that
lady pirate was piloting isn't from Ameria,

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:54.890
they still can't operate it.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.640
1010th class!
they still can't operate it.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.060
You beat the pirate!

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:02.650
You're great! You caught the lady pirate!

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.690
Oh, thank you!

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:08.150
Don't pick on someone younger than you!

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.330
Luin, the way you cover for Bellri and
try to ingratiate yourself to him,

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.540
- you sure are a Kuntala.
- Why you!

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.790
Look!

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.000
Look at that!

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.870
Step, step.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.750
That's the girl who was on the Crown, right?

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.550
Isn't that the girl who's under
Capital Army surveillance?

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.800
Woo!

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.430
- Look, Nobell's doing it too.
- ﻿1010th class rocks!

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.430
Take out those space pirates!

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.850
Manny, what's going on with her?

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.980
She's been admitted to our class.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:39.230
They want us to look after her
until her memories return.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:40.400
Is she a Kuntala?

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.480
She won't even talk about where she's from.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.860
Even though she's in good shape, physically.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:47.070
- She sure is.
- ﻿Cut that out!

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.610
Raraiya Monday isn't her real name, right?

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:52.620
They call her Monday because
that's the day she was found on.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.540
<i>﻿It's the Capital Army guys
who were on the Crown.</i>

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.830
Luin Lee, Bellri Zenam.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.540
The two I have just named are to report
to the principal's office at once.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.960
You ail take good care of her.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:07.050
- No touching!
- ﻿Huh?

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.050
It's His Holiness.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.220
- Everyone!
- Bow!

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.600
Bow.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.020
That's the girl who came from the sky?

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.740
It's because you're peeping
at her through those things.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:32.160
My apologies for that, Miss Noredo Nug.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.450
Not at all, Your Holliness.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:38.500
I can't imagine such a young girl would be...

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:56.970
So, those are the Capital Army's
Catsiths that we keep hearing about?

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:58.470
That's right.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:03.810
- ﻿I know you.
- Huh?

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:06.190
You want to go save the lady pirate
who's in Prisoner's Tower, don't you?

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:07.900
Operations Director Wilmit Zenam has arrived.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:11.530
Wha... I'm not that crazy!

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:14.700
Oh, dear. I see you've been hauled
out for this. Keep up the good work.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.200
Colonel Cumpa Rusita has arrived.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.620
- Oh, Colonel.
- Good evening.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.200
Ah, Bellri.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.790
I hear that your son captured
a pirate Mobile Suit.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.080
That's very impressive.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.540
It was a coincidence, I'm sure.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.960
He just hates losing and is quick to act.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.590
Is that right?

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:34.340
It comes from trying to live up
to my mother's expectations.

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:38.350
It would seem your disposition has a
• strong effect on your son, Director.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:39.850
Oh, not at all.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.560
Salute!

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:45.350
His Holiness has already arrived!

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:57.660
Please, be seated.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:00.740
Ah, the Operations Director has come.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.870
Why are you here this early?

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:05.120
We wanted to see the fireworks here.

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.040
That's kind of you to say.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:14.840
La, la, la, la, la! Yes!

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:19.180
This is Cumpa Rusita.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:23.270
Be courteous with our guests from the
Izanellian Continent, understood?

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:27.650
Yes, sir. The Research Division only
offers advice on world affairs.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.270
What is this static?

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.320
Space pirates?

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:35.030
It looks like someone's
spread Minovsky Particles.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.410
I'm getting nothing but static.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:41.870
Nothing but static! Nothing but static!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.120
Nobell, you be quiet!

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:49.670
What does it mean?

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.170
It's that, don't you think?

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:56.630
Home. Home.

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:59.510
When the jamming was going on,
weren't they talking about G's pilot

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:01.890
and about taking back the G?

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.310
- Huh?
- ﻿What?

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:12.110
- It's an air raid!
- ﻿They're bombing us!

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.190
- No way!
- ﻿Why?!

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:14.690
This is absurd!

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:15.780
It's gotta be the Amerians!

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.650
It's the Capital Army!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.080
The Army isn't ready yet!

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.390
Okay.

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:42.640
Hey, aren't those pirate mobile suits?

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.760
Are they going to try and
fight them on the ground?

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.390
It's crazy to try that with those Rectens.

00:07:56.190 --> 00:07:58.070
- Raraiya!
- ﻿You okay?

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.990
- Raraiya!
- Get on!

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:08.330
Prisoner's Tower or Hangar 25?!

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.750
Of course!

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:14.790
- Luin!
- Bell!

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:16.590
Ow, ow, ow...

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.260
G!

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:20.800
G's...

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.470
G! G!

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:23.720
What is she saying?

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:24.930
I don't get it.

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.240
You girls head home!

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.150
What?

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.530
We're going to Hangar 25, aren't we?

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:46.450
Did it not occur to you that they're
targeting Prisoner's Tower?

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:49.080
What are you planning to do about the canal?

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.170
Those guys...

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.760
If Bellri and Luin can do it...

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:00.840
Wha?

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.680
I'll do this with girl power!

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.850
Luin, isn't it dangerous over there?

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:15.810
I know!

00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:18.070
They haven't gotten out yet?

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.320
If so...

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:20.150
<i>﻿What about that woman?</i>

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:29.870
What? Take on the pirates in Rectens?

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.120
Bell, stop this!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:33.820
I'll go!

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.680
Aida Rayhunton!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.650
Answer me!

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:10.540
Woah!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.000
Don't get distracted by some woman!

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:15.790
Kill the lights.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.540
You're on duty, stay at your post!

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:21.590
You're already late!

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:25.550
Aren't they Amerian Mobile Suits?

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:27.260
I thought they were supposed
to be space pirates.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:29.430
- They used beam rifles in Capital Territory!
- Move forward more.

00:10:29.430 --> 00:10:30.810
Crouch down.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:39.440
They haven't said a thing, so stop
prattling on with your assumptions!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:44.240
Are there any wounded?

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.990
- These guys are insane!
- This way?

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.570
- Those Catsiths need to fight better!
- There's a fire!

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.490
- Where's the fire extinguisher?!
- ﻿Run outside!

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:51.950
You can hear me, right?

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.410
- Why can't I find it?!
- ﻿Run outside!

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:54.950
I found it! Here's the extinguisher!

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.120
- What are they doing?! It's fine as is!
- ﻿Ah, this way.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:59.210
- Bell!
- ﻿Army HQ hasn't given us orders yet!

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:00.420
Bell!

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.340
The stairs just stop?

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:13.100
- Bell.
- I bet they thought they were building a maze.

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:17.060
There are private rooms!

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:18.770
What? There's a beam of light.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.270
No way! A beam saber?

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:39.790
There's still more stairs up!

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.790
- It's down here!
- ﻿Bellri Zenam!

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.380
- Huh?
- What is it?

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:44.590
Huh?!

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:46.510
It's her!

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.310
Please, don't move!

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:01.900
Stop that!

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.270
Ow!

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:04.900
Don't stick your butt out!

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:08.360
You're nuts!

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:18.370
No, you are!

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.620
You hit me hard intentionally!

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:22.710
This is hunting slingshot ammo.

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:25.590
If I'd used it seriously,
I'd have shot a hole in your butt!

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.260
Why do you know my name?

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:33.220
You're the grade skipper
who made the G-Self move.

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:35.260
I heard about you from the investigators.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.890
You called them here, didn't you?

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:41.560
They stripped me of everything
I had. How could I?

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.190
Why is someone like you...

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:46.110
...resorting to space piracy?

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:49.650
We ought to be coating the
Earth in solar panels,

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:52.110
but the Capital prohibits it.

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:53.780
That's dictatorial!

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:54.740
Because Earth—

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:59.200
—﻿is why!

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:01.460
You...

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.860
You slapped Bell!

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:04.460
You slapped him!

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.420
We're getting out of here!

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.170
They're after her!

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:09.240
Luin!

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:11.340
Before they spread Minovsky Particles,

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:13.930
we received a transmission
demanding your return!

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:17.050
<i>﻿I knew I could count on him!
Captain Cahill came for me!</i>

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:24.650
Come on!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:27.570
Space pirates get the death penalty!

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:30.690
Luin, they say they're
getting a boat out for us.

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:32.530
Really? Good work!

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:33.740
What's the boat for?

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:35.610
You want to go to Hangar 25, right?

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:42.540
You're going to the Mobile Suit?

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.000
How could you tell?

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.670
Manny! That was careless!

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.460
We can't cross this bridge!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.130
Let's cross!

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:54.380
What?

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.050
What is that?

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:04.140
Instructor Kerbes?

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:05.440
What is this?

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.100
Hurry up and get aboard!

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:08.900
You're gonna chase off the pirates, right?

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:10.520
Of course!

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:15.450
They say they want to relocate
the pirate Mobile Suit.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.990
Okay, do it!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:18.200
Luin!

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:19.580
Manny!

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:22.790
I'm gonna fall!

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:31.170
The Army still can't move
that pirate Mobile Suit.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:34.170
And so, we got a message telling
us to get your assistance, Bellri.

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:36.880
Who did the message come from?

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.050
Captain Dellensen!

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:39.800
It was Instructor Dellensen!

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:54.030
There are civilians aboard.

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:58.700
That's Miss Aida's Iris Sign!

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:00.740
There's no mistaking it.

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:02.490
That kid is...

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:04.500
What?

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:07.620
There are two Iris Signs?

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:10.000
Miss Aida, what does this mean?

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:18.090
- ﻿It's Hangar 25!
- ﻿Yes, sir!

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:19.590
Can you see it?

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:21.100
It's Hangar 25!

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:27.980
Those guys are planning
to investigate the hangar!

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.730
- That one from earlier may come too!
- ﻿Huh?!

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:42.580
Why is there nobody here?

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.910
- Nobell's with you too?
- ﻿Is this the place?

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.330
That girl!

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.460
Bell, Noredo! Bell, Noredo!

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:52.380
Raraiya, let's get off here.

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:55.380
Is that it?

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:00.630
It's because the Army's
formation was so improvised.

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:09.850
- Huh?
- What is it?

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:13.270
What?

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:16.400
It looks the same as when I got out of it.

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:17.900
It's the G-Self.

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:19.110
Why?

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:21.360
Because that's the name I gave it.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.240
The hatch is still open too.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.500
- What?
- ﻿That's why we came here!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:32.500
Luin, start up the engine on that barge!

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:33.670
Yes, sir!

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:36.250
Bellri, get that thing moving!

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.550
Huh?!

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:41.510
Yes, sir!

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.270
The G-Self and my lady!

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:03.820
Assembly?

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:05.870
No, Recten maintenance.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.330
That woman!

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:18.750
Someone brought it.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:19.710
Raraiya?

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:23.500
Bellri! Shove her off!

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.220
I can't shove her off!

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:34.440
I can make it!

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:44.950
I can move it too, you know!

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:07.640
A collection of classics from a past era?

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:10.640
Rayhunton Code confirmed.

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:11.890
You...!

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:13.640
I set the backpack.

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:16.520
Universal Multi-Contact Setup.

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:19.650
When this recording played, I was thrown out.

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:22.690
<i>﻿But it moved.</i>

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:24.110
<i>﻿Even though neither Captain Cahill,</i>

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:26.610
<i>﻿nor Klim Nick could do it?</i>

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:29.120
Backpack fix.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.450
Ah! This looks like it's okay!

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:32.790
Doesn't it?

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:34.910
Y-Yes!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:38.420
Giovanni, you handle the next one over.

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:40.130
Yes, sir, Captain Cahill!

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:47.640
Luin, won't we stand out if we go out there?

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.680
We're going to be found either way.

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:53.010
The Minovsky Particles are
getting in the way again!

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.810
Is the girl in your custody
able to speak yet?

00:18:55.810 --> 00:18:58.810
She hasn't spoken. She hasn't spoken. Right?

00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:01.840
Someone...

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:03.820
Someone...

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:06.570
Why would a backpack you installed here work?

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:10.200
It's all built to the International Standard.
Of course it would work.

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.910
Cahill! Where are you?

00:19:26.550 --> 00:19:28.010
That's the G-Self, isn't it?

00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:34.890
Aida! My lady!

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:38.730
- Cahill!
- ﻿It's him!

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:44.480
Could Miss Aida control it
while carrying that backpack?

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:45.690
It's hostile!

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:49.110
Bell!

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:53.700
A Catsith?!

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:10.630
I can't let it fall into the Capital's hands!

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:17.350
You'd beat your own comrade to death?!

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:28.280
My lady!

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.130
Give him back!

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:49.920
Revive Captain Cahill
and give him back to me!

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:52.630
You've killed a man who didn't need to die!

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.180
I didn't kill him...

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:57.680
The Captain was a man who could
have led the Amerian Army!

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.350
He was passionate, yet gentle.

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:01.190
He was a wonderful adult!

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:03.900
What's that girl's problem?

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:06.270
There's no way Bell would kill anyone.

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:09.490
Yeah, and this is their own
fault for attacking us.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:11.400
Pa... Pa!

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:13.160
Pa...

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:15.370
Pa! Pa!

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:18.330
It was just one shot.

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:21.750
The insides are totally fried.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:24.630
Bell says he did it while protecting her.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:27.590
And that's what he gets for it?

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:35.510
Return that cockpit to the way it was.

00:21:35.510 --> 00:21:38.470
And bring Cahill back to life!

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:40.350
You were able to fight Cahill.

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:42.640
You should be able to do that much, right?!

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:44.140
Bellri Zenam!

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:46.770
That's just not possible.

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.080
Yes, I read you, Captain Dellensen.

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:03.080
Please, head here straight away.

00:22:03.080 --> 00:22:06.080
Huh? What did you say?

00:22:06.080 --> 00:22:08.500
I said we consented to it!

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:11.340
People from the Research Division
are coming too?

00:24:00.990 --> 00:24:03.830
It's not because I fell in love with
the lady pirate at first sight.

00:24:03.830 --> 00:24:07.160
I headed out because a Captain of
the Research Division called me.

00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:10.750
When there was an attack to rescue
the lady pirate on that day,

00:24:10.750 --> 00:24:13.090
I tried to head out in the G-Self...

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:14.380
and couldn't do it.

00:24:14.380 --> 00:24:16.670
It's because Miss Aida had piloted it.

00:24:17.630 --> 00:24:20.300
On the next episode of Reconguista in G,

00:24:20.300 --> 00:24:22.300
The Pressure of Montero.

00:24:22.300 --> 00:24:24.850
Even if you can't bear to wait, wait!
